00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:59.090
We all wanted it to be done in one take for him.
我们都希望这能为他一次过。

457
00:20:59.230 --> 00:20:59.590
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

458
00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:04.710
Well, Jenna, at one minute, 35 seconds, we all helped Michael up from the ground.
那么，珍娜，在一分三十五秒时，我们都帮迈克尔从地上站了起来。

459
00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:08.910
And there was absolutely no way they could crop out my belly.
而且他们绝对没有办法把我的肚子裁掉。

460
00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:11.370
And I am full pregnant in the shot.
而且我在镜头里正怀着孕。

461
00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:13.030
It is hilarious to me.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

462
00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.590
I couldn't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

463
00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.630
I laughed out loud when I saw it.
我看到的时候忍不住笑出声来。

464
00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:18.010
There was just no way.
真的是一点办法也没有。

465
00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:19.030
It's a split second.
就那么一瞬间。

466
00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:22.050
But my big old belly is right there.
但我那个大肚子就在那儿。

467
00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:25.850
Also, Angela, we have a fan catch from Yonina L.
另外，安吉拉，我们收到了来自约妮娜·L的粉丝提问。

468
00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:29.610
At one minute, 26 seconds, she would like to know,
在一分二十六秒时，她想知道，

469
00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:32.330
are you covering your mouth to stop from laughing?
你是不是在捂着嘴忍笑？

470
00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:33.710
She caught you.
她抓包你了。

471
00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:34.350
Probably.
很可能吧。

472
00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:36.410
I knew I couldn't ruin this take.
我知道我不能毁了这个镜头。

473
00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:39.670
We got a laugh catch and a belly catch in one scene.
我们一个场景里既抓到了笑场，又抓到了孕肚。

474
00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:40.390
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

475
00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:41.630
In one scene.
就在一个场景里。

476
00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:45.910
Well, after he has placed his face in the cement,
好吧，在他把脸按进水泥里之后，

477
00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:48.010
Michael has a wonderful talking head.
迈克尔有一段精彩的单独访谈。

478
00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:51.750
And he just wants you to know that today wasn't just about him.
他只是想让你们知道，今天不只是为了他自己。

479
00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:55.030
It's about his grandkids, his great grandkids.
这是为了他的孙辈、他的重孙辈。

480
00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:57.190
They can come back in 100 years.
他们可以在一百年后回来。

481
00:21:57.650 --> 00:22:01.710
And he can say, look, kids, your daddy left that face hole.
而他可以说，看哪，孩子们，你们的爸爸留下了那个脸洞。

482
00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:05.470
And that's really the gift you want to give your kids and grandkids, right?
这确实是你想要给你的孩子和孙辈的礼物，对吧？

483
00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:06.370
It's a face hole.
一个脸洞。

484
00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:06.810
Yeah.
是啊。

485
00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:08.530
Look, kids, that's my face hole.
看啊，孩子们，那是我的脸洞。

486
00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:13.810
All I could think about was the number of people who were going to trip in that face hole
我满脑子想的都是会有多少人在离开大楼时

487
00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:14.870
as they left the building.
被那个脸洞绊倒。

488
00:22:15.070 --> 00:22:17.230
It's just going to become like a rain puddle.
它只会变成像水坑一样的东西。

489
00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:18.070
Yeah.
是啊。

490
00:22:18.410 --> 00:22:19.090
Oh, Michael.
哦，迈克尔。

491
00:22:19.090 --> 00:22:22.250
Well, now we're into the episode.
好了，现在我们进入这一集了。

492
00:22:22.790 --> 00:22:25.910
Angela and Andy are doing Mad Libs.
安吉拉和安迪在玩填词游戏。

493
00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:27.090
In the kitchen.
在厨房里。

494
00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:27.790
Yeah.
是啊。

495
00:22:28.170 --> 00:22:31.470
Angela is delighted to be spending this time with Andy.
安吉拉很高兴能和安迪度过这段时间。

496
00:22:31.670 --> 00:22:32.930
She's having the best time.
她正过得最开心呢。

497
00:22:33.190 --> 00:22:36.970
Well, I think what we learn in this scene is that Angela loves a Mad Lib.
嗯，我想我们在这个场景中了解到的是，安吉拉非常喜欢填词游戏。

498
00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:37.650
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

499
00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:38.710
Who would have thought?
谁能想到呢？

500
00:22:39.010 --> 00:22:44.630
I don't know if it necessarily is Andy that she's delighted by or just the idea of a Mad Lib.
我不知道她高兴究竟是因为安迪，还是仅仅因为填词游戏这个点子。

501
00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:46.050
Maybe a little of both.
也许两者都有点吧。

502
00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:46.550
Maybe.
也许吧。

503
00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:49.150
So I went to the script, Jenna.
所以我查了剧本，珍娜。

504
00:22:49.330 --> 00:22:54.170
I went to my shooting draft to see if this scene was written the way we did it.
我翻看了我的拍摄剧本，想看看这场戏是不是按照我们演的那样写的。

505
00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:56.110
It is up until one point.
有一点是一样的。

506
00:22:56.270 --> 00:23:00.970
And then there was an extra couplet that I remember us filming because Ed was so funny.
然后多了一组对白，我记得我们拍过，因为埃德当时太搞笑了。

507
00:23:01.030 --> 00:23:02.230
And I'm so bummed.
我太难过了。

508
00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:04.870
It's not even in the deleted scenes on the DVD commentary.
DVD评论音轨的已删减片段里甚至都没有。

509
00:23:04.870 --> 00:23:06.590
And I'm going to share it with you.
我要把它分享给你。

510
00:23:06.810 --> 00:23:09.830
So in the episode, Andy reads the Mad Lib.
所以在这一集里，安迪念了疯狂填词游戏。

511
00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:14.890
And it reads, the tall man entered the nice building to visit a very nice man.
上面写着，高个子男人走进漂亮的建筑去拜访一个非常好的男人。

512
00:23:15.150 --> 00:23:16.590
Sit down, Mr. Smith.
请坐，史密斯先生。

513
00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:18.830
Could I interest you in any good cat food?
有什么好猫粮能引起您的兴趣吗？

514
00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:21.730
And Angela says, a man eating cat food.
然后安吉拉说，一个吃猫粮的男人。

515
00:23:21.850 --> 00:23:24.050
And Andy says, a cat eating man food.
然后安迪说，一个吃人粮的猫。

516
00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:25.170
And they giggle.
然后他们咯咯地笑了。

517
00:23:25.390 --> 00:23:25.650
Right?
对吧？

518
00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:26.310
Yeah.
对。

519
00:23:26.310 --> 00:23:27.790
Well, the scene would have continued.
好吧，这场戏本该继续的。

520
00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:32.630
Andy starts pantomiming being a cat eating a hamburger.
安迪开始用哑剧模仿一只吃汉堡的猫。

521
00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:35.090
And he goes, meow, a burger.
他说，喵，一个汉堡。

522
00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:37.610
Ed was so funny doing this, Jenna.
埃德做这个动作太搞笑了，珍娜。

523
00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:42.430
And then I would have responded, a cat eating a hamburger sandwich?
然后我本该回答，一只吃汉堡三明治的猫？

524
00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:43.910
That's impossible.
这不可能。

525
00:23:44.170 --> 00:23:46.190
And then Andy goes, I know.
然后安迪说，我知道。

526
00:23:46.190 --> 00:23:49.050
And I say, where do you think of these things?
我说，你怎么能想出这些东西的？

527
00:23:49.290 --> 00:23:50.390
And we laugh.
然后我们笑了。

528
00:23:51.390 --> 00:23:51.990
Amazing.
太棒了。

529
00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:54.490
A cat eating a hamburger sandwich.
一只吃汉堡三明治的猫。

530
00:23:54.490 --> 00:24:01.870
I'm really sad that you didn't get to hear that or see Ed pretending to be a cat eating a hamburger.
我真的很遗憾你没能听到或者看到埃德假装成一只吃汉堡的猫。

531
00:24:02.650 --> 00:24:10.750
Well, Angela, Justin told me that Gene and Lee actually wrote this Mad Lib scene for Angela and Andy.
好吧，安吉拉，贾斯汀告诉我吉恩和李其实是专门为安吉拉和安迪写了这场疯狂填词游戏的戏。

532
00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:12.710
So all of that was Gene and Lee.
所以所有这些都是吉恩和李写的。

533
00:24:12.990 --> 00:24:14.750
Well, it was so fun to do.
演起来真的太有趣了。

534
00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:21.110
I became inspired by this scene, Angela, to do a deep dive on Mad Libs.
安吉拉，这场戏激发了我的灵感，让我对疯狂填词游戏进行了一次深入研究。

535
00:24:21.110 --> 00:24:22.170
Oh, no.
噢，不。

536
00:24:22.510 --> 00:24:23.530
What'd you find?
你发现了什么？

537
00:24:23.830 --> 00:24:24.750
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

538
00:24:24.990 --> 00:24:26.250
It is fascinating.
太迷人了。

539
00:24:26.730 --> 00:24:28.430
Well, our kids love Mad Libs.
我们的孩子很喜欢疯狂填词游戏。

540
00:24:28.510 --> 00:24:29.850
I mean, Jenna, I did them growing up.
我是说，珍娜，我从小就玩。

541
00:24:29.950 --> 00:24:30.790
We still do them.
我们现在还在玩。

542
00:24:31.130 --> 00:24:31.630
Same.
我也是。

543
00:24:31.930 --> 00:24:33.910
Let me tell you the history of Mad Libs.
让我来告诉你疯狂填词游戏的历史。

544
00:24:34.130 --> 00:24:34.310
Okay.
好的。

545
00:24:34.670 --> 00:24:41.810
Mad Libs was invented in 1953 by two men, Leonard Stern and Roger Price.
疯狂填词游戏是1953年由伦纳德·斯特恩和罗杰·普莱斯这两位男士发明的。

546
00:24:42.190 --> 00:24:45.790
Roger Price had worked as a writer on The Bob Hope Show.
罗杰·普莱斯曾担任《鲍勃·霍普秀》的编剧。

547
00:24:46.210 --> 00:24:49.670
Leonard Stern was his friend who worked as a writer on The Honeymooners.
伦纳德·斯特恩是他的朋友，曾在《蜜月期》担任编剧。

548
00:24:49.670 --> 00:24:51.210
They were comedy writers.
他们都是喜剧编剧。

549
00:24:51.870 --> 00:24:59.170
One day, Roger went to visit Leonard at work, and Leonard was working on a script for The Honeymooners.
有一天，罗杰去伦纳德工作的地方探班，当时伦纳德正在为《蜜月期》写剧本。

550
00:24:59.330 --> 00:25:05.830
He was trying to figure out the right word to describe the nose of Ralph Cramden's new boss.
他正试图找出合适的词来形容拉尔夫·克拉姆登新老板的鼻子。

551
00:25:05.830 --> 00:25:12.010
Before he could explain the whole thing, he just said to his friend, I need an adjective.
在他解释完整件事情之前，他只是对他的朋友说，我需要一个形容词。

552
00:25:12.430 --> 00:25:16.590
And Price jumped in and started throwing out words like clumsy, naked.
然后普莱斯插话进来，开始蹦出诸如笨拙的、赤裸的之类的词。

553
00:25:16.870 --> 00:25:18.350
He just started throwing out adjectives.
他只是开始说出各种形容词。

554
00:25:18.870 --> 00:25:21.310
So, they thought this was so funny, right?
所以，他们觉得这太有趣了，对吧？

555
00:25:21.450 --> 00:25:24.210
Like, oh, a clumsy nose, a naked nose.
比如，哦，一个笨拙的鼻子，一个赤裸的鼻子。

556
00:25:24.430 --> 00:25:28.750
So, this gave them the idea to write a bunch of stories with missing words.
所以，这让他们萌生了写一堆空出词语的故事的想法。

557
00:25:29.030 --> 00:25:31.770
They took them to a cocktail party with their friends.
他们把这些带到一个鸡尾酒会上，和他们的朋友们一起玩。

558
00:25:31.890 --> 00:25:35.010
They had people fill in the blanks without knowing the context.
他们在不知道上下文的情况下让人们填空。

559
00:25:35.250 --> 00:25:37.190
And it was a huge hit.
结果大受欢迎。

560
00:25:37.430 --> 00:25:38.910
People thought this was a hoot.
人们觉得这太逗了。

561
00:25:39.150 --> 00:25:42.650
They tried to get these stories published, but publishers passed.
他们试图把这些故事出版，但出版商拒绝了。

562
00:25:42.830 --> 00:25:43.550
Nobody wanted them.
没人想要它们。

563
00:25:43.850 --> 00:25:45.090
They said, we don't get it.
他们说，我们不懂这是什么意思。

564
00:25:45.090 --> 00:25:47.530
Maybe sell it to a game company or something.
也许卖给游戏公司什么的吧。

565
00:25:47.690 --> 00:25:48.850
It sounds like a party game.
听起来像个派对游戏。

566
00:25:49.410 --> 00:25:52.010
So, they sat on the idea for five years.
于是，这个想法被他们搁置了五年。

567
00:25:52.810 --> 00:25:55.110
And then they decided to self-publish.
然后他们决定自己出版。

568
00:25:55.390 --> 00:25:57.770
But now they needed a name for it, right?
但现在他们需要为它起个名字，对吧？

569
00:25:57.930 --> 00:25:58.070
Yeah.
是的。

570
00:25:58.150 --> 00:25:59.170
They had all their stories.
他们有了所有的故事。

571
00:25:59.390 --> 00:26:00.310
They're self-publishing.
他们要自己出版了。

572
00:26:00.670 --> 00:26:01.430
Get this.
你听我说。

573
00:26:01.710 --> 00:26:04.550
These two guys, they're out having breakfast in New York.
这两个家伙在纽约吃早餐。

574
00:26:04.790 --> 00:26:09.390
And they overheard an agent arguing with his client at another table.
他们无意中听到一个经纪人在另一张桌子旁和他的客户争吵。

575
00:26:09.830 --> 00:26:13.930
And the agent was trying to tell this actor that he had to recite a certain script
那个经纪人试图告诉这个演员，他必须背诵某个剧本

576
00:26:13.930 --> 00:26:15.530
for an upcoming interview.
为了即将到来的采访。

577
00:26:15.630 --> 00:26:19.410
And the actor was saying, no, I want to ad-lib my interview.
而那个演员说，不，我想在采访中即兴发挥。

578
00:26:19.570 --> 00:26:20.690
I want to ad-lib it.
我想即兴发挥。

579
00:26:20.850 --> 00:26:24.750
And the agent said, that would be mad to ad-lib an interview.
经纪人说，在采访中即兴发挥简直疯了。

580
00:26:25.030 --> 00:26:27.670
And that's where the name Mad Lib came from.
这就是“疯狂填词”（Mad Lib）这个名字的由来。

581
00:26:27.810 --> 00:26:33.750
And now they have sold over 110 million copies of Mad Lib's books.
现在他们已经售出了超过1.1亿册“疯狂填词”的书籍。

582
00:26:33.970 --> 00:26:35.410
That was amazing.
太精彩了。

583
00:26:35.410 --> 00:26:37.930
I loved every single moment of that.
我喜欢其中的每一个瞬间。

584
00:26:37.930 --> 00:26:43.410
But I also find it really inspiring that you can have this once-in-a-lifetime idea
但我也觉得这真的很鼓舞人心，你可以拥有这样一个千载难逢的想法

585
00:26:43.990 --> 00:26:47.530
and, you know, don't let go of it, even if it takes you six years,
而且，你知道的，不要放弃它，哪怕花了你六年时间，

586
00:26:47.750 --> 00:26:49.990
to see it come, like, to fruition.
看着它最终实现，比如，修成正果。

587
00:26:50.570 --> 00:26:50.970
Yeah.
是的。

588
00:26:51.130 --> 00:26:54.090
They were on to something and they knew it and they made it happen.
他们发现了什么，他们心知肚明，并且将其变成了现实。

589
00:26:54.290 --> 00:26:55.070
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

590
00:26:55.210 --> 00:26:55.990
Great deep dive.
精彩的深度剖析。

591
00:26:56.450 --> 00:26:56.850
Thanks.
谢谢。

592
00:26:57.410 --> 00:26:57.930
All right.
好的。

593
00:26:58.030 --> 00:26:59.950
Well, now Michael's going to come out of his office.
那么，现在迈克尔要从他的办公室出来了。

594
00:26:59.950 --> 00:27:03.730
And immediately, he's going to clock Pam and her glasses.
并且他会立刻注意到潘和她的眼镜。

595
00:27:04.530 --> 00:27:06.690
And he says to her, you know what?
他对她说，你知道吗？

596
00:27:06.790 --> 00:27:09.670
In order to get hotter, you've got to take off those glasses.
为了变得更性感，你得摘下那副眼镜。

597
00:27:09.930 --> 00:27:11.450
She's just going in the wrong direction.
她简直是在往错误的方向发展。

598
00:27:12.090 --> 00:27:12.410
Yes.
是的。

599
00:27:12.590 --> 00:27:17.270
And Pam tries to explain to Michael what happened, why she's wearing these glasses.
然后潘试图向迈克尔解释发生了什么，她为什么戴着这些眼镜。

600
00:27:17.270 --> 00:27:21.070
And he has this line that people quote to me all the time.
他有句台词，人们总是拿来对我说。

601
00:27:21.250 --> 00:27:25.110
He's like, it's noise coming out of an ugly scientiSt.
他就像是在说，这不过是个丑陋的科学家发出的噪音。

602
00:27:26.910 --> 00:27:27.390
Michael.
迈克尔。

603
00:27:28.010 --> 00:27:29.150
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

604
00:27:29.150 --> 00:27:32.770
That was really hard for me to get through every time Steve said that.
每次史蒂夫说那句话，我都觉得好难忍住不笑。

605
00:27:33.050 --> 00:27:33.510
I bet.
我敢说确实如此。

606
00:27:34.050 --> 00:27:36.250
I feel like I've seen that on a t-shirt, Jenna.
珍娜，我觉得我好像在T恤上见过那句话。

607
00:27:36.610 --> 00:27:37.210
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

608
00:27:38.750 --> 00:27:39.610
Oh, you have.
哦，你肯定见。过

609
00:27:40.130 --> 00:27:42.150
Imagine for someone who's never seen the office
想象一下，对于一个从没看过《办公室》的人来说

610
00:27:42.150 --> 00:27:44.970
and then, like, sees someone in these t-shirts, like,
然后，比如说，看到有人穿着印有这种话的T恤，比如

611
00:27:45.250 --> 00:27:46.550
Dwight, you ignorant slut.
德怀特，你这个无知的荡妇。

612
00:27:46.950 --> 00:27:49.250
It's just noise coming out of an ugly scientiSt.
这不过是个丑陋的科学家发出的噪音而已。

613
00:27:49.670 --> 00:27:54.170
I feel like the office has given some really random clothing choices for people.
我觉得《办公室》给人们提供了很多奇奇怪怪的服装选择。

614
00:27:54.350 --> 00:27:56.090
Well, when I got my glasses in real life
对了，当我在现实生活中配了眼镜

615
00:27:56.090 --> 00:27:59.610
and I posted my first picture on Instagram of myself in my new glasses,
并在Instagram上发了第一张戴着新眼镜的照片时

616
00:28:00.130 --> 00:28:02.790
people started putting all of these comments.
人们开始留下各种各样的评论。

617
00:28:03.190 --> 00:28:05.770
They were like, you're going in the wrong direction.
他们说，你这是在走下坡路啊。

618
00:28:05.950 --> 00:28:08.370
You have to take off your glasses to get hotter.
你得把眼镜摘了才能变好看。

619
00:28:08.770 --> 00:28:11.530
And then other people were like, it's noise coming out of it.
然后其他人就说，这不过是噪音发出来的。

620
00:28:11.530 --> 00:28:12.410
I was so offended.
我当时气坏了。

621
00:28:12.870 --> 00:28:15.470
I forgot about this scene in the office.
我都把《办公室》里的这一幕给忘了。

622
00:28:15.830 --> 00:28:18.210
And I was like, why is everybody coming down on me?
我还心想，怎么每个人都在针对我？

623
00:28:18.330 --> 00:28:20.030
I thought my glasses were cute.
我觉得我的眼镜挺可爱的呀。

624
00:28:20.750 --> 00:28:21.430
I know.
我懂。

625
00:28:21.590 --> 00:28:22.270
I so relate.
我太有同感了。

626
00:28:22.410 --> 00:28:26.190
One time I posted a photo early in my Instagram days in a green sweater.
有一次，我还在用Instagram不久的时候，发了一张穿着绿色毛衣的照片。

627
00:28:26.350 --> 00:28:29.050
And someone was like, looking a little whorish, aren't we?
然后有人评论说，看着有点风骚啊，是吧？

628
00:28:29.250 --> 00:28:31.930
And I was like, wow, how rude.
我当时就想，哇，怎么这么粗鲁。

629
00:28:32.610 --> 00:28:34.070
And then I was like, oh, right.
然后我才反应过来，哦，对。

630
00:28:34.210 --> 00:28:34.830
Green is whorish.
绿色就是很风骚。

631
00:28:34.830 --> 00:28:35.470
OK, OK.
行吧，行吧。

632
00:28:35.590 --> 00:28:35.830
Got it.
懂了。

633
00:28:35.870 --> 00:28:36.070
Got it.
懂了。

634
00:28:36.110 --> 00:28:36.350
Got it.
懂了。

635
00:28:36.890 --> 00:28:37.410
I know.
我知道。

636
00:28:37.550 --> 00:28:38.390
Sometimes I forget.
有时候我都忘了。

637
00:28:38.410 --> 00:28:40.910
I'm actually grateful that we're doing this rewatch
我其实很庆幸我们现在在重温这部剧

638
00:28:40.910 --> 00:28:44.810
because I feel like I'm less likely to be offended by comments now
因为我觉得我现在没那么容易被评论冒犯了

639
00:28:44.810 --> 00:28:46.490
because they're actually quotes.
因为这些评论其实都是台词梗。

640
00:28:46.970 --> 00:28:48.670
Well, after all the insults,
好了，在经历了这一堆侮辱之后

641
00:28:48.810 --> 00:28:51.430
Michael tells everyone to go into the conference room
迈克尔让大家去会议室

642
00:28:51.430 --> 00:28:53.350
for a brainstorming session.
开个头脑风暴会议。

643
00:28:54.150 --> 00:28:54.770
Oh, lady.
哦，天哪。

644
00:28:55.050 --> 00:28:57.290
There is a scene between Jim and Pam
吉姆和潘之间有一场戏

645
00:28:57.290 --> 00:28:59.310
that is not in this episode.
这一集里并没有播。

646
00:28:59.310 --> 00:29:01.010
And it's not in the deleted scene.
而且删减片段里也没有。

647
00:29:01.010 --> 00:29:03.510
So you have to tell me if you guys film this.
所以你们得告诉我，你们当时到底拍没拍过这个。

648
00:29:03.510 --> 00:29:04.810
It's kind of racy.
这剧情有点大尺度。

649
00:29:05.030 --> 00:29:05.810
You want to hear it?
想听吗？

650
00:29:06.330 --> 00:29:06.890
What?
什么？

651
00:29:07.430 --> 00:29:09.770
So I'm reading the shooting draft last night.
所以昨晚我在读拍摄剧本。

652
00:29:09.910 --> 00:29:11.130
And this is in there.
然后里面有这么一段。

653
00:29:11.430 --> 00:29:13.010
As people head to the conference room,
当大家走向会议室时，

654
00:29:13.290 --> 00:29:14.790
Jim smiles at Pam.
吉姆朝帕姆微微一笑。

655
00:29:15.130 --> 00:29:18.210
Jim says, the price you pay for a night in heaven.
吉姆说，共度天堂一夜的代价。

656
00:29:18.930 --> 00:29:20.050
Oh, wait.
噢，等等。

657
00:29:20.710 --> 00:29:23.430
Pam glances at the camera, stilted.
帕姆瞥了一眼镜头，显得很不自然。

658
00:29:24.170 --> 00:29:27.070
Yes, the movies were good, Jim.
没错，电影挺好看的，吉姆。

659
00:29:27.790 --> 00:29:31.830
Jim says, you mean the movies that we made of us making love?
吉姆说，你是说我们做爱时拍的那些电影吗？

660
00:29:35.430 --> 00:29:37.830
Glances to camera, shut up.
瞥向镜头，闭嘴吧。

661
00:29:38.070 --> 00:29:39.450
We didn't film ourselves.
我们才没有拍自己呢。

662
00:29:40.110 --> 00:29:43.210
Jim to camera, hi, Pam's grandma.
吉姆对着镜头说，嗨，帕姆的奶奶。

663
00:29:43.590 --> 00:29:45.070
Sorry you had to find out like this.
很抱歉让你以这种方式发现。

664
00:29:45.230 --> 00:29:48.670
And then Pam hits Jim and they go into the conference room.
然后帕姆打了吉姆一下，他们走进了会议室。

665
00:29:49.210 --> 00:29:49.530
What?
什么？

666
00:29:50.830 --> 00:29:53.510
I don't remember if we filmed that.
我不记得我们拍过那个。

667
00:29:53.710 --> 00:29:55.990
If it's in the shooting draft, we must have.
如果拍摄剧本里有，那我们肯定拍过。

668
00:29:56.410 --> 00:29:59.410
People would have lost their minds if we'd left that in the show.
如果把那段留在剧里，观众们肯定会疯掉的。

669
00:29:59.410 --> 00:30:00.550
I know.
我知道。

670
00:30:01.010 --> 00:30:02.590
Like, what the heck?
就觉得，搞什么鬼？

671
00:30:02.770 --> 00:30:05.850
I read it last night and I was like, like I did a spit take.
我昨晚读到的时候，简直，差点把水喷出来。

672
00:30:06.010 --> 00:30:07.650
I was like, what's happening with Jim and Pam?
我就想，吉姆和帕姆这到底是怎么了？

673
00:30:08.010 --> 00:30:12.130
Just hearing that makes me feel like I've just walked in on my parents.
光是听到这段，就让我感觉像是不小心撞见我爸妈。

674
00:30:12.330 --> 00:30:12.990
I know.
我懂。

675
00:30:13.530 --> 00:30:14.870
Having an intimate moment.
在进行亲密时刻。

676
00:30:15.230 --> 00:30:16.490
Like, I was just like, no, no, no.
当时我就觉得，不，不，不。

677
00:30:16.670 --> 00:30:17.390
Don't want to see it.
一点也不想看。

678
00:30:17.510 --> 00:30:18.210
Don't want to see it.
一点也不想看。

679
00:30:18.770 --> 00:30:21.710
Which is probably why it was edited out.
这大概就是为什么它被剪掉了。

680
00:30:21.870 --> 00:30:24.050
But it cracked me up reading it.
不过我读到的时候快笑死了。

681
00:30:24.870 --> 00:30:25.270
Wow.
哇。

682
00:30:26.890 --> 00:30:28.570
Well, there you go, guys.
好吧，就是这样，各位。

683
00:30:28.910 --> 00:30:29.610
There you go.
就是这样。

684
00:30:29.750 --> 00:30:33.630
Now we're in the conference room and the actual scene they leave in between the two of you guys
现在我们来到了会议室，他们俩之间实际保留下来的那场戏

685
00:30:34.150 --> 00:30:37.170
is Jim proposing to Pam, which is also in the script.
是吉姆向帕姆求婚，剧本里也是这么写的。

686
00:30:37.330 --> 00:30:41.770
So I guess if they had to choose one, that one is a little bit more in character for you guys.
所以我想如果必须二选一的话，那场戏跟你们两个的人设更符合一点。

687
00:30:42.150 --> 00:30:45.210
Well, proposing that I go get him some more coffee.
好吧，其实是提议我去给他多拿杯咖啡。

688
00:30:45.470 --> 00:30:46.370
Right, right, right.
对，对，对。

689
00:30:46.550 --> 00:30:47.490
But you're doing the face.
但你当时做了那个表情。

690
00:30:47.710 --> 00:30:50.150
You know, he's now doing this bit with you, right?
你知道的，他现在在跟你开这个玩笑，对吧？

691
00:30:50.790 --> 00:30:51.190
Yeah.
对。

692
00:30:51.190 --> 00:30:57.410
Well, Michael has written the words energize in block letters on a piece of paper up front.
迈克尔在前方的纸上用醒目的大写字母写了“激发活力”几个字。

693
00:30:57.670 --> 00:31:02.470
And he wants to know how can we energize the office?
他想知道我们该如何给办公室注入活力？

694
00:31:02.870 --> 00:31:04.950
A few people are throwing out ideas.
几个人开始出谋划策。

695
00:31:05.210 --> 00:31:10.730
Andy suggests that we have a new outgoing message, something with zing and pep.
安迪建议我们换个新的外拨留言，要带点活力和干劲的那种。

696
00:31:11.230 --> 00:31:17.130
Jim suggests we have an even better message with more zing and more pep.
吉姆建议我们弄个更好的留言，要有更多活力和更多干劲。

697
00:31:17.550 --> 00:31:20.070
Michael wants to get Stanley's opinion.
迈克尔想听听斯坦利的意见。

698
00:31:20.070 --> 00:31:21.750
Stanley's not having it.
斯坦利根本不买账。

699
00:31:21.870 --> 00:31:23.070
He's like, not me.
他的态度就是，别找我。

700
00:31:23.370 --> 00:31:24.310
He's not interested.
他一点兴趣都没有。

701
00:31:24.410 --> 00:31:25.690
He's not even answering him.
他甚至都不理他。

702
00:31:25.850 --> 00:31:26.350
I know.
我知道。

703
00:31:26.530 --> 00:31:29.590
And Michael keeps pushing and pushing and pushing.
而且迈克尔一直在不停地逼迫。

704
00:31:29.990 --> 00:31:32.470
And that is when he says the line,
然后就在那时，他说出了那句台词：

705
00:31:33.030 --> 00:31:35.090
Did I stutter?
我刚才结巴了吗？

706
00:31:35.850 --> 00:31:37.470
And everyone is stunned.
所有人都惊呆了。

707
00:31:37.810 --> 00:31:40.710
We're like, whoa, this just took a turn.
我们在想，哇，事情大条了。

708
00:31:41.330 --> 00:31:44.110
Michael excuses himself for a glass of water.
迈克尔借口去喝杯水离开了。

709
00:31:44.710 --> 00:31:45.210
Oof.
噢。

710
00:31:45.210 --> 00:31:45.930
Oof.
噢。

711
00:31:46.410 --> 00:31:54.810
Now, Jenna, per Justin Spitzer, this is the only episode title that was an actual line in the script.
詹娜，根据贾斯汀·斯皮策的说法，这是唯一一个剧集标题直接出自剧本台词的剧集。

712
00:31:55.550 --> 00:31:55.870
Yes.
没错。

713
00:31:56.030 --> 00:32:00.270
Justin said he had originally thought they should call it insubordination.
贾斯汀说他最初觉得应该叫《抗命不尊》。

714
00:32:00.630 --> 00:32:00.990
Oh.
哦。

715
00:32:01.370 --> 00:32:03.310
But they settled on Did I stutter?
但他们最终敲定为《我刚才结巴了吗？》。

716
00:32:03.510 --> 00:32:05.150
Well, I like Did I stutter better.
嗯，我更喜欢《我刚才结巴了吗？》。

717
00:32:05.490 --> 00:32:05.990
Me too.
我也是。

718
00:32:06.870 --> 00:32:15.990
Next up, we're in Michael's office and Toby is sitting with him and he's trying to tell Michael that he needs to talk with Stanley about his insubordination.
接下来，我们在迈克尔的办公室里，托比正和他坐在一起，试图告诉迈克尔，他需要找斯坦利谈谈其抗命不尊的问题。

719
00:32:15.990 --> 00:32:23.890
And once again, Toby is in Michael's corner and Michael just refuses to see Toby as someone who could be there for him.
而这一次，托比是站在迈克尔这边的，但迈克尔就是拒绝把托比看作是一个能支持他的人。

720
00:32:24.330 --> 00:32:24.470
Yeah.
是啊。

721
00:32:24.630 --> 00:32:30.470
He tries to tell Toby that he misinterpreted what he saw, that they were actually a couple of pals.
他试图告诉托比，是他误解了自己看到的景象，他们其实是一对好哥们。

722
00:32:30.630 --> 00:32:31.810
They're kind of joshing around.
他们当时只是在开玩笑打闹。

723
00:32:32.250 --> 00:32:36.230
Toby wouldn't know because Toby doesn't have friends, Michael says.
迈克尔说，托比不会懂的，因为托比根本没有朋友。

724
00:32:36.570 --> 00:32:36.790
Yeah.
没错。

725
00:32:37.110 --> 00:32:40.190
If you had a friend, you would say something like this.
如果你有个朋友，你就会说这样的话。

726
00:32:40.550 --> 00:32:42.090
Hey, you're poor.
嘿，你是个穷光蛋。

727
00:32:42.290 --> 00:32:44.150
Well, hey, your mom is dead.
好吧，嘿，你妈死了。

728
00:32:44.370 --> 00:32:45.390
That's what friends do.
这才是朋友会做的事。

729
00:32:46.310 --> 00:32:47.930
So there you go, Toby.
所以就是这样，托比。

730
00:32:48.210 --> 00:32:49.390
Get some friends.
去交几个朋友吧。

731
00:32:49.650 --> 00:32:55.470
But it's clear at the end of this meeting that Michael is going to be expected to do something about what happened.
但很显然，这次会议快结束时，迈克尔注定得为发生的事情采取点行动。

732
00:32:55.710 --> 00:32:58.170
It's also clear that Michael's really anxious about it.
同样明显的是，迈克尔对此真的感到非常焦虑。

733
00:32:58.250 --> 00:32:59.610
He says he has a stomach ache.
他说他肚子疼。

734
00:33:00.130 --> 00:33:00.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

735
00:33:01.010 --> 00:33:02.870
And Jenna, there's a deleted scene.
而且詹娜，这里有一个被删减的片段。

736
00:33:03.310 --> 00:33:04.890
It's so great.
太棒了。

737
00:33:05.110 --> 00:33:10.350
First of all, it shows the geography of Dunder Mifflin in a whole new way that we've never seen before.
首先，它以一种我们从未见过的方式展现了邓德米夫林的整个地理布局。

738
00:33:10.710 --> 00:33:15.270
So in this deleted scene, there's a talking head and it's over the action.
所以在剪掉的这个片段里，有一个画外采访，声音是直接叠在画面上的。

739
00:33:15.390 --> 00:33:16.210
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吧？

740
00:33:16.370 --> 00:33:19.990
And Michael is talking about how him and Stanley are friends.
迈克尔正在说他和斯坦利是朋友。

741
00:33:20.170 --> 00:33:22.510
In fact, Stanley is one of his oldest friends.
事实上，斯坦利是他最老的朋友之一。

742
00:33:22.790 --> 00:33:27.370
But while he's saying all this, he's walking out of his office and he clearly has to go pee.
但就在他说这些话的时候，他走出了办公室，而且明显是尿急。

743
00:33:27.410 --> 00:33:30.050
And he sees Stanley and he pivots hard right.
然后他看到了斯坦利，立刻来了个急转弯。

744
00:33:30.050 --> 00:33:37.190
He goes out the front door of Dunder Mifflin, past the elevators, to the stairwell door next to Vance Refrigeration.
他走出了邓德米夫林的正门，经过电梯，来到万斯冷气公司旁边的楼梯间门口。

745
00:33:37.310 --> 00:33:46.730
He goes down the stairs, out the front door of Dunder Mifflin, through the parking lot, to a back door that's another stairwell, up those stairs.
他走下楼梯，出了邓德米夫林的正门，穿过停车场，来到后门另一个楼梯间，然后走上那些楼梯。

746
00:33:46.730 --> 00:33:50.730
And he comes out by the break room, by the venting machines.
他从自动售货机旁的休息室旁边走了出来。

747
00:33:50.830 --> 00:33:55.350
And then he walks through the annex, into the kitchen, into the men's room.
接着他穿过副办公室，走进厨房，再走进男洗手间。

748
00:33:55.890 --> 00:34:01.730
That's what he did because he had to go pee and he did not want to walk past Stanley's desk.
这就是他做的事，因为他想去小便，而他根本不想从斯坦利的办公桌前走过。

749
00:34:02.430 --> 00:34:02.710
Wow.
哇。

750
00:34:02.710 --> 00:34:09.950
And we've never seen anyone in the run of the show come up the back stairwell into the area where the break room is.
而且在整部剧的播出期间，我们从来没见过任何人从后楼梯上来，走到休息室所在的区域。

751
00:34:10.210 --> 00:34:10.950
That's right.
没错。

752
00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:12.790
I loved it just visually.
单从视觉效果上我就很喜欢。

753
00:34:13.150 --> 00:34:17.030
And that shows you the extremes he was going to to avoid Stanley.
这说明为了躲避斯坦利，他可谓无所不用其极。

754
00:34:17.530 --> 00:34:27.190
Well, now we're going to get into the B storyline of this episode, which is that Andy is selling his car, his Xterra, and Dwight is going to buy it.
好了，现在我们要进入本集的B线剧情了，也就是安迪在卖他的车，他的Xterra，而德怀特打算买下它。

755
00:34:27.310 --> 00:34:29.970
His Xterra when he was driving a Prius.
他明明开着一辆普锐斯，却还要买Xterra。

756
00:34:30.090 --> 00:34:31.710
So I don't know what's happening here.
所以我搞不懂这到底是闹哪出。

757
00:34:31.710 --> 00:34:32.910
I know.
就是说啊。

758
00:34:33.410 --> 00:34:34.570
What's that about?
这算怎么回事？

759
00:34:35.150 --> 00:34:35.770
You know what?
你知道吗？

760
00:34:35.830 --> 00:34:38.210
In my mind, it was like his old car from college.
在我看来，这就好像是他在大学时的旧车一样。

761
00:34:38.650 --> 00:34:39.030
Hmm.
嗯。

762
00:34:39.510 --> 00:34:40.250
Maybe so.
也许吧。

763
00:34:40.650 --> 00:34:41.670
From his Cornell days.
从他康奈尔大学的时期开始。

764
00:34:42.190 --> 00:34:45.650
Well, we had a fan question from Barbara G and Rebecca H.
好了，我们收到了来自芭芭拉·G和丽贝卡·H的粉丝提问。

765
00:34:45.790 --> 00:34:51.170
At 6 minutes 45 seconds, Dwight points out that there's a scratch on Andy's Xterra.
在6分45秒时，德怀特指出安迪的Xterra上有个划痕。

766
00:34:51.370 --> 00:34:58.790
In a deleted scene from safety training, Angela, you might remember, Angela keys Andy's car.
在《安全培训》的一段删减戏里，安吉拉——你们可能还记得——安吉拉划了安迪的车。

767
00:34:58.790 --> 00:35:01.830
Did Angela also key his Xterra?
安吉拉也划了他的Xterra吗？

768
00:35:02.210 --> 00:35:04.170
I don't think so.
我觉得没有。

769
00:35:04.330 --> 00:35:06.090
I think she just keyed the Prius.
我觉得她划的只是那辆普锐斯。

770
00:35:06.390 --> 00:35:12.650
But in the script, you guys, Angela is watching all of this interaction between Dwight and Andy.
不过在剧本里，各位，安吉拉一直在观察德怀特和安迪之间的所有这些互动。

771
00:35:12.650 --> 00:35:16.810
She is perhaps titillated by it, fascinated, curious.
她可能对此感到兴奋、着迷、好奇。

772
00:35:16.990 --> 00:35:20.350
But there are several scenes where she's peering through the window.
有好几场戏里她都在透过窗户窥视。

773
00:35:20.690 --> 00:35:23.830
The camera busts her at one point and she gets agitated.
镜头有一次当场抓包了她，她显得有些慌乱。

774
00:35:23.830 --> 00:35:28.110
So she is sort of watching all of this all day long.
所以她整天都在暗中观察这一切。

775
00:35:28.590 --> 00:35:36.570
Well, Dwight ends up bullying Andy into selling him the car at a very low rate, way under asking.
总之，德怀特最后软硬兼施，逼得以极低的价格把车卖给他，远低于要价。

776
00:35:36.850 --> 00:35:38.950
He does that thing where he's like, do it.
他就用了那一招，说什么，照做吧。

777
00:35:39.150 --> 00:35:39.530
Sell it.
卖掉它。

778
00:35:39.710 --> 00:35:40.210
Give it to me.
把它给我。

779
00:35:40.390 --> 00:35:41.050
Say yes now.
现在就说好。

780
00:35:41.290 --> 00:35:41.890
Say yes now.
现在就说好。

781
00:35:42.010 --> 00:35:44.890
Three, two, one, five, four, three.
三，二，一，五，四，三。

782
00:35:45.310 --> 00:35:46.150
Say yes.
说好。

783
00:35:46.890 --> 00:35:48.050
And it works.
然后这招管用了。

784
00:35:48.350 --> 00:35:49.390
He says, OK.
他说，好吧。

785
00:35:49.850 --> 00:35:51.570
Now, here's an interesting tidbit.
现在有个有趣的八卦。

786
00:35:51.730 --> 00:35:57.010
This car, this Xterra, actually belonged to our hairdresser, Kim Ferry.
这辆车，这辆Xterra，实际上属于我们的发型师金·费里。

787
00:35:57.310 --> 00:35:59.130
And she was actually selling it.
她当时确实在卖这辆车。

788
00:35:59.330 --> 00:36:00.130
She was.
没错。

789
00:36:00.370 --> 00:36:01.510
It was so crazy.
太疯狂了。

790
00:36:01.770 --> 00:36:04.290
She let us borrow her car for this episode.
她把车借给我们拍这一集。

791
00:36:04.290 --> 00:36:05.670
And then she sold it.
然后她把它卖了。

792
00:36:06.270 --> 00:36:07.830
Just like these guys.
就像这俩人一样。

793
00:36:08.450 --> 00:36:19.130
Well, I guess Michael is going to finally baby step up to Stanley's desk and he's basically going to forgive Stanley before Stanley has even apologized.
好吧，我想迈克尔终于要小心翼翼地走到斯坦利的办公桌前了，而且基本上是在斯坦利甚至还没道歉之前就原谅了斯坦利。

794
00:36:19.670 --> 00:36:28.930
But the way he approaches Stanley really reminds me of like when my kids want something, but they don't want to ask me and they just come and stand by you and kind of hover.
但他接近斯坦利的方式真的很让我想起我的孩子们想要什么东西的时候，他们又不好意思开口，于是就过来站在你旁边，磨磨蹭蹭的。

795
00:36:29.250 --> 00:36:29.570
Yeah.
对。

796
00:36:29.770 --> 00:36:34.710
He's just standing next to Stanley's desk and Stanley's like, yeah, what do you want?
他只是站在斯坦利的桌子旁，斯坦利就问，干嘛，你想要什么？

797
00:36:35.410 --> 00:36:35.970
Yeah.
对。

798
00:36:36.130 --> 00:36:37.810
And he's like, you know, nothing.
然后他说，你知道的，没什么。

799
00:36:37.810 --> 00:36:40.710
I think I just want to say like we're cool, right?
我想我只是想说，我们没事了吧，对吧？

800
00:36:40.930 --> 00:36:42.370
Like I forgive you.
就好像我原谅你了一样。

801
00:36:42.610 --> 00:36:45.730
And we've forgotten about what happened.
而我们却把发生过的事给忘了。

802
00:36:46.170 --> 00:36:46.590
Right?
对吧？

803
00:36:46.950 --> 00:36:47.410
Yeah.
对。

804
00:36:48.010 --> 00:36:50.710
Now, Stanley could just say yes.
现在，斯坦利完全可以说“好”。

805
00:36:50.930 --> 00:36:51.570
I know.
我知道。

806
00:36:51.850 --> 00:36:53.030
But he does not.
但他没有。

807
00:36:53.370 --> 00:36:57.810
I think Stanley has had years of putting up with Michael and he's just had it.
我觉得斯坦利忍受迈克尔已经很多年了，他现在是彻底受够了。

808
00:36:58.230 --> 00:36:58.610
Yeah.
对。

809
00:36:58.610 --> 00:37:09.210
Since that didn't work, Michael is going to sit with Dwight and try to figure out, is there a way that someone else might be able to discipline Stanley?
既然这招行不通，迈克尔就打算和德怀特坐下来商量，看看有没有什么办法让别人来管教一下斯坦利？

810
00:37:09.590 --> 00:37:13.250
Does Stanley report to anyone else besides Michael?
除了迈克尔，斯坦利还向其他人汇报工作吗？

811
00:37:13.690 --> 00:37:20.730
And this is when Dwight gets out his very extensive, very hilarious employee org chart.
就在这个时候，德怀特拿出了他那份内容详尽、极其搞笑的员工组织结构图。

812
00:37:20.970 --> 00:37:22.470
It's so elaborate.
做得太精致了。

813
00:37:22.470 --> 00:37:24.430
It was really well made.
真的制作得很精良。

814
00:37:24.430 --> 00:37:28.290
He has a, like, tripod he sets it on.
他甚至还拿了个三脚架把图表支在上面。

815
00:37:28.510 --> 00:37:30.090
There's like an overlay.
上面还有透明覆盖层呢。

816
00:37:30.590 --> 00:37:32.990
I mean, Jenna, this thing was not cheap.
我是说，珍娜，这东西可不便宜。

817
00:37:33.310 --> 00:37:44.170
Well, Brent told us that the entire writing staff put a huge amount of time and effort into that org chart and that they had the idea that after this episode,
嗯，布伦特告诉我们，整个编剧团队在这张组织结构图上投入了大量的时间和精力，他们当时还盘算着，等这集播出后，

818
00:37:44.310 --> 00:37:47.770
NBC could sell the org chart as posters.
全国广播公司可以把这张组织结构图当成海报来卖。

819
00:37:47.770 --> 00:37:53.970
So they filled it with all these little jokes that you can't even really spot in the episode itself.
所以他们在里面塞了各种各样的小笑话，你在正片里甚至都很难注意到。

820
00:37:54.210 --> 00:38:00.630
And unfortunately, though, the poster did not become the runaway bestseller they had hoped it would be.
不过遗憾的是，这张海报并没有像他们期望的那样成为畅销爆款。

821
00:38:00.970 --> 00:38:07.990
However, Kent Sabornak sent me a picture of it and we will put it in the pod so you can really unpack it if you'd like.
不过，肯·萨博纳克发给我一张照片，我们会把它放到播客里，如果你想的话可以仔细研究一下。

822
00:38:07.990 --> 00:38:13.910
Yeah, I looked at that last night and the detail of the menstruation cycles of the women.
对，我昨晚看了，上面还有女员工经期周期的细节呢。

823
00:38:14.490 --> 00:38:17.210
You know, Dwight has shared that he clocks all of that.
你知道的，德怀特曾说过他把这些都记录下来了。

824
00:38:17.390 --> 00:38:18.350
Well, he wasn't kidding.
好吧，他可不是在开玩笑。

825
00:38:18.870 --> 00:38:20.790
Angela, we got a fan question about this scene.
安吉拉，我们收到了一条关于这个场景的粉丝提问。

826
00:38:20.930 --> 00:38:26.610
At 9 minutes, 34 seconds, did Rain improvise touching Michael's face with his pointer?
在9分34秒的时候，雷恩是用指挥棒触碰迈克尔的脸这一幕是即兴发挥吗？

827
00:38:27.710 --> 00:38:28.230
Yes.
是的。

828
00:38:29.130 --> 00:38:30.090
Yes, he did.
是的，他是即兴发挥的。

829
00:38:30.090 --> 00:38:32.210
And they could not get through it.
他们当时根本拍不下去。

830
00:38:32.210 --> 00:38:40.570
They were cracking up something so sort of delicate and intimate about Dwight touching Michael's face with that metal pointer.
他们笑得不行，德怀特用金属指挥棒触碰迈克尔的脸这个动作，有一种说不出的微妙和亲密感。

831
00:38:40.970 --> 00:38:44.610
And those two fellas were just disintegrating into laughter.
然后这两个家伙就笑得前仰后合。

832
00:38:44.850 --> 00:38:45.810
It's in the bloopers.
花絮里有这一段。

833
00:38:46.030 --> 00:38:47.270
It's so fun to watch.
看起实在是太好玩了。

834
00:38:47.830 --> 00:38:54.430
Justin said before they started the scene, they had to decide whether or not Rain would have that metal pointer or a laser pointer.
贾斯汀说在开拍这场戏之前，他们得决定雷恩是拿那个金属指挥棒还是激光笔。

835
00:38:54.950 --> 00:38:56.530
And he's so glad.
他太庆幸了。

836
00:38:56.710 --> 00:38:59.390
I'm so glad they gave him the metal pointer.
我也庆幸他们给了他金属指挥棒。

837
00:38:59.750 --> 00:38:59.910
Yeah.
对。

838
00:38:59.910 --> 00:39:05.690
Brent said that after Rain improvised it once, they loved it and they had him do it again.
布伦特说，在雷恩即兴发挥了一次后，大家都非常喜欢，于是让他又演了一遍。

839
00:39:05.790 --> 00:39:11.550
And it took over seven takes before they got even three seconds of usable footage.
结果拍了七次以上，才勉强得到了三秒钟能用的镜头。

840
00:39:11.730 --> 00:39:15.330
And that's what you see in the episode was like take number eight.
正片里你看到的差不多是第八条。

841
00:39:15.990 --> 00:39:19.490
Well, back at reception, Kevin is complimenting Pam's glasses.
好了，镜头回到前台，凯文正在称赞潘的眼镜。

842
00:39:19.750 --> 00:39:21.410
I mean, they're kind of a turn on for him.
我是说，这对他来说有点像是一种挑逗。

843
00:39:22.330 --> 00:39:24.410
Jenna, there's a lot more in the script.
珍娜，剧本里其实还有很多内容。

844
00:39:24.750 --> 00:39:27.650
In fact, Kevin says you're basically in his league now.
事实上，凯文说你现在基本上和他是一个级别的了。

845
00:39:28.730 --> 00:39:31.310
So I think there were a few alts for this scene.
所以我觉得这场戏拍了好几个备选版本。

846
00:39:31.530 --> 00:39:33.010
I remember shooting it.
我记得当时在拍的时候。

847
00:39:33.170 --> 00:39:34.770
We were laughing so hard.
我们笑得太厉害了。

848
00:39:35.130 --> 00:39:39.550
There's also that famous line where he says, can you say these are due back Thursday?
其中还有一句很著名的台词，他说，你能说这些书周四到期吗？

849
00:39:39.930 --> 00:39:42.050
And Pam's like, no, no.
然后潘说，不行，不行。

850
00:39:42.710 --> 00:39:52.490
At nine minutes, 58 seconds at the very top of this interaction between Pam and Kevin, I want you to know that John is actively playing free cell on his computer.
在9分58秒，也就是潘和凯文这场对手戏的刚开始，我想让你们知道，约翰当时其实正在电脑上玩空当接龙。

851
00:39:52.750 --> 00:39:53.750
Oh, I saw it.
哦，我看到了。

852
00:39:53.830 --> 00:39:55.250
It's not just on his computer.
这不只在他的电脑上。

853
00:39:55.430 --> 00:39:56.950
You can see him moving the car.
你能看到他在挪动那辆车。

854
00:39:57.210 --> 00:39:57.690
Oh, no.
哦，不。

855
00:39:57.810 --> 00:39:58.850
He's full on playing.
他完全是在玩。

856
00:39:59.550 --> 00:40:06.290
But this interaction between Kevin and Pam is going to cause Pam to take her glasses off now for the rest of the day.
但凯文和帕姆之间的这次互动，将导致帕姆在今天剩下的时间里把眼镜摘下来。

857
00:40:06.470 --> 00:40:07.010
She's done.
她不干了。

858
00:40:07.190 --> 00:40:08.270
She's sick of the comments.
她受够了那些评论。

859
00:40:08.590 --> 00:40:10.370
She's just going to not see.
她干脆选择什么也看不见。

860
00:40:11.070 --> 00:40:13.590
But how bad is this woman's vision?
但这个女人的视力到底有多差？

861
00:40:13.590 --> 00:40:20.310
Because she takes her glasses off and then Jenna, the phone rings and she has a hard time finding the handle of the phone.
因为她摘下了眼镜，然后珍娜，电话铃响了，她很难找到话筒的手柄。

862
00:40:20.310 --> 00:40:23.970
There is a talking head that did not make it in the episode.
有一个没能在正片中播出的单人访谈。

863
00:40:24.170 --> 00:40:24.750
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

864
00:40:25.170 --> 00:40:29.370
Where Pam says that her vision is 20 slash 400.
帕姆在访谈里说她的视力是20比400。

865
00:40:29.770 --> 00:40:35.490
I'll have you know, Angela, legal blindness is anything that's 20 slash 200 or worse.
安吉拉，我得告诉你，法定盲人标准是20比200或更糟。

866
00:40:35.730 --> 00:40:40.650
So Pam would be considered legally blind without her glasses or contacts.
所以如果不戴眼镜或隐形眼镜，帕姆会被视为法定盲人。

867
00:40:40.650 --> 00:40:51.010
And basically what it means is that Pam can see things 20 feet away, but normal people could see that same thing 400 feet away.
基本上这意味着帕姆在20英尺外能看到的东西，正常人从400英尺外就能看到。

868
00:40:51.190 --> 00:40:55.250
So it doesn't really track that Pam can't see the phone.
所以帕姆看不到电话这一点其实有点说不通。

869
00:40:56.130 --> 00:41:00.490
What it should mean is that she can't see Stanley anymore.
这本来应该意味着她再也看不到斯坦利了。

870
00:41:00.710 --> 00:41:00.910
Okay.
好吧。

871
00:41:01.450 --> 00:41:01.730
Yeah.
是的。

872
00:41:02.430 --> 00:41:06.830
So maybe we didn't research her eyesight properly.
所以也许我们没有好好研究过她的视力。

873
00:41:08.090 --> 00:41:12.130
But in general, though, all of her vision would be fairly blurry.
不过总的来说，她的视线应该会相当模糊。

874
00:41:12.370 --> 00:41:13.890
I do remember researching that.
我确实记得研究过这个。

875
00:41:14.350 --> 00:41:18.790
Well, I thought you played it so well, Jenna, because that's not an easy thing to play.
好吧，我觉得你演得太棒了，珍娜，因为这并不是一个好演的桥段。

876
00:41:19.030 --> 00:41:22.750
And the physicality of your comedy in this episode is fantastic.
而且你在这集里的喜剧肢体语言太棒了。

877
00:41:23.310 --> 00:41:24.790
Well, thank you very much.
非常感谢。

878
00:41:25.050 --> 00:41:25.350
Yes.
没错。

879
00:41:26.070 --> 00:41:32.270
Well, guys, Michael's going to go down to the warehouse and try to get maybe some advice on how to deal with Stanley.
好了，各位，迈克尔要下去仓库，想试着讨教一些如何对付斯坦利的建议。

880
00:41:32.270 --> 00:41:39.250
But before we go there, let's take a break and then we'll come back to learn a little bit about Fluffy Fingers.
但在我们去那之前，先休息一下，然后回来了解一点关于“毛茸茸的手指”的故事。

881
00:41:50.580 --> 00:41:51.820
Okay, guys, we're back.
好的，各位，我们回来了。

882
00:41:51.960 --> 00:41:56.280
And as promised, we're going to break down this scene between Michael and Daryl.
正如我们承诺的，我们要剖析迈克尔和达里尔之间的这场戏。

883
00:41:56.540 --> 00:41:57.780
It's amazing.
太棒了。

884
00:41:58.140 --> 00:41:59.660
Everything about it is amazing.
这其中的一切都太棒了。

885
00:41:59.660 --> 00:42:04.640
Even just from a technical standpoint, this was such a tiny, tiny room.
甚至单从技术角度来看，这是一个非常非常小的房间。

886
00:42:04.960 --> 00:42:09.980
And Randall had to shoot through the door in a window and capture this moment.
兰多尔必须透过门上的窗户拍摄并捕捉这个瞬间。

887
00:42:10.160 --> 00:42:11.300
It's so beautifully done.
拍得太美了。

888
00:42:11.300 --> 00:42:16.520
And Michael's going to ask Daryl, hey, man, have you ever been in a gang?
然后迈克尔要问达里尔，嘿，老兄，你加入过帮派吗？

889
00:42:17.100 --> 00:42:21.980
And Daryl needs to know what Michael needs to say.
而达里尔需要知道迈克尔想说什么。

890
00:42:22.200 --> 00:42:22.540
Yeah.
对。

891
00:42:22.680 --> 00:42:27.700
So he says he has been in not just one gang, but several.
所以他说他加入的不仅是一个帮派，而是好几个。

892
00:42:28.240 --> 00:42:28.460
Yeah.
对。

893
00:42:28.780 --> 00:42:33.940
He has been in the Crips and the Bloods and the Warriors and the Newsies.
他加入过瘸帮、血帮、勇士帮和报童帮。

894
00:42:34.220 --> 00:42:35.880
And the Newsies on Broadway.
还有百老汇的报童帮。

895
00:42:37.480 --> 00:42:40.320
And Michael is just like, oh, my God.
而迈克尔简直就是，天哪。

896
00:42:40.720 --> 00:42:41.080
Yeah.
是的。

897
00:42:41.880 --> 00:42:42.980
Oh, my God.
天哪。

898
00:42:43.340 --> 00:42:50.140
And Michael can't believe that Daryl is now about to share with him his, like, deep gang knowledge.
迈克尔简直不敢相信达里尔现在要跟他分享他那些所谓的深厚帮派知识。

899
00:42:51.020 --> 00:42:51.240
Yeah.
没错。

900
00:42:51.460 --> 00:42:54.800
What do you do if you're disrespected in the gang?
如果你在帮派里被不尊重了，你该怎么办？

901
00:42:55.340 --> 00:42:58.680
Daryl's going to tell him they do something called Fluffy Fingers.
达里尔打算告诉他，他们有一种叫作“毛茸茸的手指”的招数。

902
00:42:58.680 --> 00:43:03.600
And that is where you surprise the person by tickling them.
那就是你通过胳肢对方来给他们一个惊喜。

903
00:43:03.820 --> 00:43:04.300
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

904
00:43:04.660 --> 00:43:09.120
And you keep tickling them until they start to tickle you.
然后你一直胳肢他们，直到他们开始反过来胳肢你。

905
00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:11.320
And then you're just tickling each other.
接着你们就互相胳肢对方。

906
00:43:11.580 --> 00:43:11.920
Yeah.
是啊。

907
00:43:11.920 --> 00:43:13.180
And then you're over it.
然后这事儿就过去了。

908
00:43:13.520 --> 00:43:15.300
It's really effective, he says.
他说，这真的非常有效。

909
00:43:15.520 --> 00:43:17.100
And Michael's like, wow.
迈克尔听了就觉得，哇。

910
00:43:17.520 --> 00:43:22.980
I didn't think that's how it went in the gangs.
我没想到帮派里的规矩是这样的。

911
00:43:23.000 --> 00:43:23.720
But okay.
不过好吧。

912
00:43:24.220 --> 00:43:24.780
Okay.
好吧。

913
00:43:25.340 --> 00:43:26.040
Michael's like, all right.
迈克尔就想，好吧。

914
00:43:26.040 --> 00:43:28.420
I guess I should try this.
我想我应该试试这个。

915
00:43:28.420 --> 00:43:29.500
It's so great.
这太棒了。

916
00:43:29.500 --> 00:43:32.240
And both Steve and Craig play it perfectly.
而且史蒂夫和克雷格都把这演得绝了。

917
00:43:32.600 --> 00:43:33.280
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

918
00:43:33.840 --> 00:43:38.380
Well, you know, Jenna, there was a deleted scene where Michael tries to get up the courage
你知道的，珍娜，本来有个被删减的场景是迈克尔试图鼓起勇气

919
00:43:38.380 --> 00:43:41.540
to tickle Stanley to do the Fluffy Fingers.
去胳肢斯坦利，好使出“毛茸茸的手指”。

920
00:43:41.840 --> 00:43:42.700
It's insane.
太疯狂了。

921
00:43:42.700 --> 00:43:45.280
Stanley is at the supply cabinet.
斯坦利在文具柜旁。

922
00:43:45.560 --> 00:43:47.460
He's kind of reaching up to grab something.
他正伸手去拿什么东西。

923
00:43:47.700 --> 00:43:49.360
And Michael sneaks up behind him.
然后迈克尔悄悄摸到他身后。

924
00:43:49.420 --> 00:43:52.260
And he holds his hands up like he's going to tickle him.
他把双手举起来，做出要胳肢他的样子。

925
00:43:52.480 --> 00:43:55.200
But then he just can't quite figure out how to do it.
但随后他就是不知道该怎么下手。

926
00:43:55.340 --> 00:43:56.660
And Stanley doesn't even notice.
而斯坦利甚至都没察觉。

927
00:43:56.820 --> 00:43:57.900
And Michael backs away.
接着迈克尔默默退了回去。

928
00:43:58.320 --> 00:44:02.460
And then Michael has a deleted talking head where he says, it's not Daryl's fault.
然后迈克尔有一段被删减的单采，他说，这不怪达里尔。

929
00:44:02.680 --> 00:44:04.540
It was a great idea.
这是个绝妙的主意。

930
00:44:04.880 --> 00:44:07.540
I just couldn't quite figure out how to do it.
我只是搞不懂具体该怎么做。

931
00:44:07.620 --> 00:44:08.120
I don't know.
我不知道。

932
00:44:08.340 --> 00:44:09.380
I've tried everything.
我什么都试过了。

933
00:44:09.720 --> 00:44:11.240
I'm running out of options.
我快没招了。

934
00:44:11.920 --> 00:44:12.400
Yeah.
是啊。

935
00:44:12.700 --> 00:44:16.920
And when you run out of options, you decide to fake fire someone.
而当你山穷水尽时，你就会决定假装把人解雇。

936
00:44:17.280 --> 00:44:19.260
That's what Michael does.
这就是迈克尔做的事。

937
00:44:19.920 --> 00:44:21.020
Oh, Michael.
哦，迈克尔。

938
00:44:21.600 --> 00:44:24.340
So now Ryan has arrived.
所以现在瑞恩到了。

939
00:44:24.340 --> 00:44:26.500
He pulls up in his convertible.
他开着他的敞篷车驶来。

940
00:44:26.720 --> 00:44:27.980
His shirt is open.
他的衬衫敞开着。

941
00:44:28.340 --> 00:44:30.860
He winks at himself in the rearview mirror.
他在后视镜里对自己抛了个媚眼。

942
00:44:31.160 --> 00:44:31.840
Oh, yeah.
哦，对啊。

943
00:44:31.900 --> 00:44:33.080
He's feeling real good.
他自我感觉极好。

944
00:44:33.320 --> 00:44:35.520
And there was a deleted scene, Jenna.
还有一个被删减的场景，珍娜。

945
00:44:35.740 --> 00:44:36.680
That was so good.
真的太棒了。

946
00:44:36.840 --> 00:44:37.840
He comes in the office.
他走进办公室。

947
00:44:38.040 --> 00:44:39.180
He's got bagels.
他带着百吉饼。

948
00:44:39.340 --> 00:44:41.240
But Pam doesn't have her glasses on.
但帕姆没戴眼镜。

949
00:44:41.240 --> 00:44:42.940
And he tosses a bagel at her.
然后他朝她扔了一个百吉饼。

950
00:44:43.220 --> 00:44:44.260
She can't see it.
她根本看不见。

951
00:44:44.340 --> 00:44:45.420
It hits her in the face.
这直接砸到了她脸上。

952
00:44:46.040 --> 00:44:50.380
And then he goes on, Jenna, to show Pam how to eat a bagel.
然后珍娜，他接着教潘怎么吃百吉饼。

953
00:44:50.540 --> 00:44:55.940
He just, with his own hands, starts digging out all the good part of the bagel, all the
他直接用双手，把百吉饼里所有好吃的部分都掏出来，把

954
00:44:55.940 --> 00:44:56.520
middle part.
中间的部分。

955
00:44:56.560 --> 00:45:00.480
And he says, yeah, you just eat that outer part, you know, so you don't gain weight.
然后他说，对啊，你只吃外面那一圈就行了，这样才不会发胖。

956
00:45:00.540 --> 00:45:02.020
And he kind of points to Pam's belly.
他还顺便指了指潘的肚子。

957
00:45:03.120 --> 00:45:08.080
And I felt like that whole scene showed his state of mind, how manic he is, throwing the
我觉得整场戏展现了他的精神状态，他有多狂躁，扔

958
00:45:08.080 --> 00:45:09.420
bagels, digging them apart.
百吉饼，把它们掰开。

959
00:45:09.480 --> 00:45:10.940
Like, oh, my gosh.
真是的，我的天啊。

960
00:45:11.180 --> 00:45:12.600
I remember shooting that.
我还记得拍这场戏的时候。

961
00:45:12.780 --> 00:45:14.900
I was sad it didn't make it in because that was really fun.
没能剪进正片里我挺难过的，因为那真的很有趣。

962
00:45:15.320 --> 00:45:16.620
You were so good in it.
你在里面演得太好了。

963
00:45:16.700 --> 00:45:18.960
I mean, he's like he tosses a bagel at you.
我是说，他就像是把百吉饼朝你扔过去。

964
00:45:19.080 --> 00:45:21.560
And Jenna, I really believed you didn't see it.
珍娜，我是真的觉得你没看到。

965
00:45:22.540 --> 00:45:24.320
That's how good you are in the scene.
这就是你在戏里演得有多好。

966
00:45:25.180 --> 00:45:26.900
Anyway, so Ryan is here.
总之，瑞恩来了。

967
00:45:26.960 --> 00:45:28.420
He's actually got some big business.
他其实是来谈大生意的。

968
00:45:28.420 --> 00:45:32.000
He goes in the conference room and he calls Jim in.
他走进会议室，把吉姆叫了进去。

969
00:45:32.240 --> 00:45:37.220
Toby's there and he's going to give him a formal warning about his job performance.
托比也在那儿，他要就吉姆的工作表现给他一份正式警告。

970
00:45:37.560 --> 00:45:40.180
But the way he calls him in is so amazing.
但他叫吉姆进去的方式太绝了。

971
00:45:40.440 --> 00:45:44.980
He's like, hey, Jim, Jim, I got to ask you a question as a true Eagles fan.
他说，嘿，吉姆，吉姆，我得作为一个铁杆老鹰队球迷问你个问题。

972
00:45:45.240 --> 00:45:46.480
Oh, so slimy.
噢，太油滑了。

973
00:45:46.780 --> 00:45:49.920
I thought BJ was so good in this scene.
我觉得BJ在这场戏里演得太棒了。

974
00:45:50.100 --> 00:45:53.240
He was like every douchebag I've ever had a meeting with.
他就像我遇到过的所有混蛋老板一样。

975
00:45:53.800 --> 00:45:58.200
I actually recorded it off my computer and I texted it to him.
我甚至直接从电脑上录了下来，然后发短信给他。

976
00:45:58.420 --> 00:46:01.600
And I said, BJ, we're watching Did I Stutter?
我说，BJ，我们正在看《我结巴了吗？》。

977
00:46:01.760 --> 00:46:05.400
And you are so brilliant and amazing in the scene.
你在这一场里简直天才又惊艳。

978
00:46:05.580 --> 00:46:08.560
I just needed you to watch it so you can see how good you are.
我只是需要让你看看，好让你知道自己演得有多好。

979
00:46:09.740 --> 00:46:14.340
And he wrote me back and he was like, Jenna, oh, my God, I forgot about that scene.
他回信跟我说，珍娜，天哪，我都忘掉这场戏了。

980
00:46:14.500 --> 00:46:15.680
Thank you for sending this to me.
谢谢你发给我看。

981
00:46:15.760 --> 00:46:16.940
That was so fun to watch.
看这个太有趣了。

982
00:46:17.100 --> 00:46:19.700
But that happens when we are rewatching this show.
不过当我们重看这部剧时，这种事就会发生。

983
00:46:20.080 --> 00:46:26.240
Sometimes I will see one of our friends perform just like madness level amazing.
有时候我会看到我们的某个朋友演技大爆发，简直绝了。

984
00:46:26.240 --> 00:46:27.980
And I just send it to him.
然后我就会发给他。

985
00:46:28.220 --> 00:46:31.920
I'm like, you need to be reminded of what an amazing comedic actor you are.
我会说，你得记起自己是个多么优秀的喜剧演员。

986
00:46:32.100 --> 00:46:32.760
You're welcome.
不用谢。

987
00:46:33.220 --> 00:46:33.780
Oh, for sure.
噢，确实如此。

988
00:46:33.960 --> 00:46:38.560
I had a whole text thread with Phyllis because I was like, Phyllis, you are so amazing.
我和菲莉丝有一整串聊天记录，因为我说，菲莉丝，你太棒了。

989
00:46:38.720 --> 00:46:40.080
Back in Yankee Swap.
回想一下《洋基换物》那一集。

990
00:46:40.360 --> 00:46:41.340
She's so good.
她太优秀了。

991
00:46:41.640 --> 00:46:42.280
I know.
我知道。

992
00:46:42.700 --> 00:46:44.060
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

993
00:46:44.300 --> 00:46:45.880
BJ is so good in these moments.
BJ在这些时刻表现得太好了。

994
00:46:46.360 --> 00:46:49.420
And Jim is like, is this because I talked to David Wallace?
然后吉姆就问，这是因为我和大卫·华莱士谈过话吗？

995
00:46:49.420 --> 00:46:51.280
And Ryan's like, no, no, no.
瑞恩就说，不，不，不。

996
00:46:51.420 --> 00:46:54.120
I appreciate, you know, constructive criticism.
我很感激，你知道的，建设性的批评。

997
00:46:54.340 --> 00:46:55.380
I thrive on it.
我靠这个获得成长。

998
00:46:55.560 --> 00:46:55.720
Yeah.
对啊。

999
00:46:55.940 --> 00:46:56.880
So douchey.
太渣了。

1000
00:46:57.260 --> 00:46:59.760
And he says, you can get more details from Toby.
然后他说，你可以从托比那里了解更多细节。

1001
00:47:00.180 --> 00:47:02.000
This leads to a Toby talking head.
这里切到了托比的访谈镜头。

1002
00:47:02.180 --> 00:47:04.520
And dare I say that Toby seems smug?
而且我敢说，托比看起来挺洋洋得意的？

1003
00:47:04.840 --> 00:47:06.060
Oh, for sure.
哦，绝对是。

1004
00:47:06.720 --> 00:47:06.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1005
00:47:07.140 --> 00:47:11.720
Toby says, I'd say all the goofing around at Pam's desk and hanging out with Pam has finally
托比说，我觉得在帕姆的办公桌旁胡闹、跟帕姆厮混，

1006
00:47:11.720 --> 00:47:12.440
caught up with him.
终于让他付出代价了。

1007
00:47:12.900 --> 00:47:15.060
Fans were furious, Jenna.
粉丝们当时气坏了，珍娜。

1008
00:47:15.060 --> 00:47:19.020
Jenna, when this episode came out, they hated Toby so much.
珍娜，这一集播出的时候，他们恨透了托比。

1009
00:47:19.160 --> 00:47:22.780
I mean, in the episode before, he put his hand on Pam's knee.
我是说，就在前一集，他把手放在了帕姆的膝盖上。

1010
00:47:23.100 --> 00:47:23.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1011
00:47:23.900 --> 00:47:28.460
And now it seems like he's going behind Jim's back to try to get him fired.
现在看起来他好像在背后搞吉姆的小动作，想让他被解雇。

1012
00:47:28.800 --> 00:47:29.220
Oh, yeah.
哦，对啊。

1013
00:47:29.700 --> 00:47:34.720
And Jenna, if you thought you hated Toby with that talking head, had you seen the deleted
而且珍娜，如果你觉得看那个访谈时就恨透了托比，那你看过吉姆和托比的删减片段吗？

1014
00:47:34.720 --> 00:47:36.800
scene between Jim and Toby?
然后还有瑞安，你当时肯定会觉得，天哪。

1015
00:47:37.100 --> 00:47:39.940
And then Ryan, you would have been like, oh, my God.
大家会……托比当时绝对就彻底没法翻身了。

1016
00:47:40.100 --> 00:47:43.020
People would have, Toby would not have been able to come back from it.
山姆，你能播放一下那个删减片段吗？

1017
00:47:43.160 --> 00:47:44.740
Sam, can you play that deleted scene?
正式警告，说真的。

1018
00:47:45.440 --> 00:47:46.960
A formal warning, seriously.
好吧，如你所知，多年来德怀特对你提起了很多投诉。

1019
00:47:47.560 --> 00:47:51.780
Well, as you know, Dwight has filed a lot of complaints against you over the years.
而且以前没人管。

1020
00:47:51.940 --> 00:47:52.600
And no one cared.
但现在这被视为一个生产力问题。

1021
00:47:52.920 --> 00:47:56.000
But now it's being looked at as more of a productivity issue.
生产力？

1022
00:47:56.780 --> 00:47:57.260
Productivity?
我的业绩很好。

1023
00:47:57.380 --> 00:47:58.120
My numbers are good.
我知道。

1024
00:47:58.380 --> 00:47:59.080
I know.
但瑞安觉得还不够好。

1025
00:48:00.320 --> 00:48:03.480
But Ryan thinks that they're not good enough.
华莱士喜欢吉姆。

1026
00:48:04.380 --> 00:48:05.380
Wallace likes Jim.
所以针对他，对我来说是个冒险的举动。

1027
00:48:05.580 --> 00:48:08.420
So going after him, that's a risky move for me.
但在商言商，你必须承担风险。

1028
00:48:08.800 --> 00:48:11.320
But in business, you've got to take risks.
有时候你得把车顶敞开，开上开阔的高速公路。

1029
00:48:11.880 --> 00:48:15.460
Sometimes you've got to get out on the open highway with a top down.
天哪。

1030
00:48:20.090 --> 00:48:21.650
Oh, my God.
而瑞安正试图打开他车的敞篷，结果却打不开。

1031
00:48:22.170 --> 00:48:25.650
And Ryan is trying to put the top down to his car and it won't go down.
哇。

1032
00:48:27.130 --> 00:48:27.690
Wow.
哇。

1033
00:48:28.350 --> 00:48:28.470
Wow.
不过说真的，你能想象如果保留了这些镜头会怎样吗？

1034
00:48:28.470 --> 00:48:30.830
But yeah, can you imagine if those scenes have been left in?
哦。

1035
00:48:31.550 --> 00:48:31.870
Oh.
好吧，安吉拉，说到背叛，德怀特把那辆Xterra洗干净了，现在正以9000多美元的价格转售。

1036
00:48:32.410 --> 00:48:39.910
Well, Angela, speaking of treachery, Dwight has washed the Xterra and he's now reselling it
他在转手赚差价。

1037
00:48:39.910 --> 00:48:41.490
for over $9,000.
哦，而安迪的反应是，搞什么鬼，老兄？

1038
00:48:42.270 --> 00:48:43.890
He's selling it for a profit.
安吉拉印象深刻。

1039
00:48:44.290 --> 00:48:46.750
Oh, and Andy is like, what the hell, man?
安吉拉的反应就像是，哦，好吧。

1040
00:48:47.570 --> 00:48:48.670
Angela's impressed.
嗯哼。

1041
00:48:49.310 --> 00:48:50.590
Angela's like, oh, yeah.
你拿捏住他了。

1042
00:48:50.590 --> 00:48:51.350
Mm-hmm.
你更聪明。

1043
00:48:51.810 --> 00:48:52.610
You got him.
她就喜欢两个男人为她争风吃醋。

1044
00:48:52.690 --> 00:48:53.330
You're smarter.
她真的超爱。

1045
00:48:53.810 --> 00:48:55.910
She loves two men dueling over her.
我知道。

1046
00:48:56.270 --> 00:48:57.130
She really does.
大家还记得吧，迈克尔已经走投无路了。

1047
00:48:57.350 --> 00:48:57.730
I know.
“毛茸茸的手指”这招对他不管用了。

1048
00:48:58.150 --> 00:49:00.930
You guys remember, Michael has run out of options.
所以他不得不去做那件他一直不想做的事。

1049
00:49:01.210 --> 00:49:02.910
Fluffy Fingers isn't going to work for him.
所以他不得不去做那件他一直不想做的事。

1050
00:49:03.670 --> 00:49:06.290
So he's going to have to do the thing he didn't want to do.
所以他不得不去做那件他一直不想做的事。

1051
00:49:06.550 --> 00:49:10.010
He's going to have to fake fire Stanley to teach him a lesson.
他打算假装开除斯坦利来给对方一个教训。

1052
00:49:10.270 --> 00:49:13.810
And he comes out of his office and he announces it to everyone.
然后他从办公室走出来，向所有人宣布这件事。

1053
00:49:13.970 --> 00:49:16.690
He says, guys, guys, guys, listen, I'm going to fake fire Stanley,
他说，伙计们，伙计们，听着，我要假装开除斯坦利，

1054
00:49:16.690 --> 00:49:20.310
but I just want you to react as if I'm really firing Stanley.
但我希望你们的反应就像我真的在开除斯坦利一样。

1055
00:49:20.570 --> 00:49:26.210
And everybody's like, if you hadn't told us what you were doing, we would have reacted correctly.
结果大家都在说，如果你刚才不告诉我们在做什么，我们的反应就对了。

1056
00:49:26.650 --> 00:49:29.710
And he's like, oh, my gosh, why aren't you understanding this?
而他却说，天哪，你们为什么不明白呢？

1057
00:49:29.830 --> 00:49:34.090
The person that says it, the person that's the voice of reason is Kevin.
那个说话的人，那个扮演理智声音的人是凯文。

1058
00:49:36.040 --> 00:49:39.660
You know you're in trouble when Kevin is the voice of reason.
当凯文成为理智的声音时，你就知道有麻烦了。

1059
00:49:40.080 --> 00:49:44.100
Stanley walks into the bullpen and Michael fake fires him.
斯坦利走办公区，迈克尔假装开除了他。

1060
00:49:44.100 --> 00:49:46.460
And it does not go well.
结果情况很不妙。

1061
00:49:46.740 --> 00:49:49.260
Stanley unleashes on him.
斯坦利对他发飙了。

1062
00:49:49.500 --> 00:49:52.920
Just a tirade of insults.
简直是一连串的侮辱。

1063
00:49:53.470 --> 00:49:57.140
I remember when we filmed this, Jenna, and you could have heard a pin drop.
珍娜，我记得我们拍摄这段的时候，现场鸦雀无声。

1064
00:49:57.520 --> 00:49:58.020
Yes.
是的。

1065
00:49:58.240 --> 00:50:01.780
It was such a beautifully dramatic moment.
这是一个非常精彩的戏剧性时刻。

1066
00:50:03.280 --> 00:50:04.960
Leslie crushed it.
莱斯利演得太棒了。

1067
00:50:04.960 --> 00:50:12.000
Yeah, you guys, we reached out to Leslie because we really, really wanted him to come on the pod today
对，大家，我们联系了莱斯利，因为我们真的很想让他今天来上播客，

1068
00:50:12.000 --> 00:50:17.960
because this is just a tour de force storyline and performance by him in this episode.
因为他在这一集里的故事线和表演简直是一场精湛的演技巅峰。

1069
00:50:18.360 --> 00:50:21.040
And he is filming this week.
他这周正在拍戏。

1070
00:50:21.240 --> 00:50:24.540
He is filming something and he couldn't come on.
他在拍一部作品，所以没能来。

1071
00:50:24.640 --> 00:50:28.060
But he did want us to share with you that this monologue was completely scripted.
但他确实想让我们告诉大家，这段独白是完全按照剧本演的。

1072
00:50:28.220 --> 00:50:29.340
This was not improvised.
这不是即兴发挥。

1073
00:50:29.340 --> 00:50:37.120
You know, and I remember, Angela, that he worked on this and he delivered it like it was just an amazing performance.
安吉拉，我记得他为此下了功夫，他的台词功底就像是一场精彩绝伦的演出。

1074
00:50:37.140 --> 00:50:38.600
And he nailed it every take.
而且他每次拍摄都一条过。

1075
00:50:38.800 --> 00:50:39.380
Every take.
每一次都一条过。

1076
00:50:39.560 --> 00:50:41.480
He was 100% off book.
他台词背得滚瓜烂熟。

1077
00:50:41.600 --> 00:50:43.620
He showed up ready to throw it down.
他做好了全力以赴的准备来到现场。

1078
00:50:43.840 --> 00:50:47.760
And we were just all so happy for him.
我们都为他感到高兴。

1079
00:50:48.100 --> 00:50:49.420
This moment was amazing.
这个时刻太棒了。

1080
00:50:49.420 --> 00:50:52.040
And I remember us all applauding at the end of the scene.
我记得我们在场景结束时都鼓掌了。

1081
00:50:52.520 --> 00:50:52.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1082
00:50:52.940 --> 00:50:54.480
Well, Michael throws everybody out.
接着，迈克尔把所有人都赶了出去。

1083
00:50:54.480 --> 00:50:57.540
He yells and says, everybody get out.
他大喊着说，所有人出去。

1084
00:50:57.740 --> 00:50:58.960
Everybody except Stanley.
除了斯坦利，所有人。

1085
00:50:59.240 --> 00:50:59.820
Everybody out.
全部出去。

1086
00:51:00.080 --> 00:51:02.160
And everyone gets the hell out.
每个人都慌不择路地跑了出去。

1087
00:51:02.380 --> 00:51:07.880
And Jenna, in the script, which isn't in the deleted scenes, but in the script,
珍娜，在剧本里——这不在被删减的片段里，但在剧本里——

1088
00:51:08.240 --> 00:51:12.580
Michael turns to the cameras and says, you two cameras out of here.
迈克尔转向摄像机说，你们两个摄像机也给我滚出去。

1089
00:51:12.800 --> 00:51:13.360
Everybody.
所有人。

1090
00:51:13.840 --> 00:51:14.400
Wow.
哇。

1091
00:51:14.780 --> 00:51:20.900
And that's why at 18 minutes, 17 seconds, you see the cameras sneak back in.
这就是为什么在18分17秒时，你会看到摄像机又悄悄溜了回来。

1092
00:51:21.040 --> 00:51:24.160
It's because in the script, Michael told them to get out.
因为在剧本里，迈克尔让他们滚出去。

1093
00:51:24.480 --> 00:51:25.960
I loved that move.
我喜欢这个桥段。

1094
00:51:26.360 --> 00:51:34.560
I loved it because when Michael is alone with Stanley or thinks he's alone with Stanley, he gets really vulnerable.
我喜欢它，因为当迈克尔独自面对斯坦利，或者以为自己和斯坦利独处时，他会变得非常脆弱。

1095
00:51:34.800 --> 00:51:36.160
There's tears in his eyes.
他的眼里含着泪水。

1096
00:51:36.300 --> 00:51:38.960
And he says, why do you pick on me?
他说，你为什么总是针对我？

1097
00:51:39.320 --> 00:51:41.520
Like, why do you pick on me like this?
就像，你为什么非要这样针对我？

1098
00:51:41.660 --> 00:51:43.120
And it's really vulnerable.
那真的是一种脆弱的展现。

1099
00:51:43.640 --> 00:51:47.300
And Stanley, very matter of fact, he says, I don't respect you.
而斯坦利非常实事求是地说，我不尊重你。

1100
00:51:47.300 --> 00:51:56.680
And then I felt like Michael had such an honest moment that could not have happened if the cameras were there, where he says, fine, I accept that.
然后我觉得迈克尔有一个非常坦诚的时刻，如果摄像机在场的话是绝不可能发生的，他说道，好吧，我接受这一点。

1101
00:51:56.840 --> 00:51:58.020
You don't respect me.
你对我不尊重。

1102
00:51:58.180 --> 00:51:59.280
I accept it.
我接受。

1103
00:51:59.380 --> 00:52:02.660
But you can't talk to me like that here.
但你不能在这里这样对我说话。

1104
00:52:03.120 --> 00:52:04.500
I am your boss.
我是你的老板。

1105
00:52:04.740 --> 00:52:06.500
And it just cannot be done.
而且这绝对不行。

1106
00:52:06.500 --> 00:52:08.560
And I agree with you, Angela.
我同意你的看法，安吉拉。

1107
00:52:08.940 --> 00:52:15.880
Anytime Michael knows the cameras are there, he can't help but perform in some way for them.
只要迈克尔知道镜头在拍，他就忍不住要在镜头前表现一番。

1108
00:52:16.440 --> 00:52:23.180
And so I feel like we're seeing a side of Michael Scott that can only be seen when he doesn't know the cameras are there.
所以我感觉我们看到了迈克尔·斯科特只有在不知道镜头在拍时才会展现的一面。

1109
00:52:23.860 --> 00:52:24.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1110
00:52:24.020 --> 00:52:31.520
And that was such a fun part of our show, playing with who are our characters when we know the cameras are there and when we don't.
这也是我们节目非常有趣的一部分，探讨当知道镜头在拍和不知道镜头在拍时，我们的角色都是什么样子的。

1111
00:52:31.660 --> 00:52:36.920
And I loved that we got to reveal these little different parts of ourselves in these different ways.
我喜欢我们能以各种不同的方式展现出自己不同的小侧面。

1112
00:52:37.360 --> 00:52:38.280
Oh, me too.
哦，我也是。

1113
00:52:38.300 --> 00:52:40.460
It made the show so rich, right?
这让节目变得如此丰富，对吧？

1114
00:52:40.720 --> 00:52:41.340
It's cool.
很酷。

1115
00:52:41.520 --> 00:52:42.280
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1116
00:52:42.400 --> 00:52:43.820
They have this moment of resolution.
他们有这样一个达成和解的时刻。

1117
00:52:44.120 --> 00:52:45.060
They're like, fine.
他们好像在说，好吧。

1118
00:52:45.060 --> 00:52:47.500
We now know our rules of engagement, right?
我们现在知道了彼此的交往规则，对吧？

1119
00:52:47.740 --> 00:52:48.020
Yeah.
对。

1120
00:52:48.140 --> 00:52:48.980
They shake hands.
他们握手。

1121
00:52:49.160 --> 00:52:49.600
Done.
搞定。

1122
00:52:50.160 --> 00:52:52.560
This leads to Michael having a talking head.
这引出了迈克尔的一段单采。

1123
00:52:52.560 --> 00:52:53.760
He's really stuck.
他真的陷进去了。

1124
00:52:54.020 --> 00:52:57.820
On the idea of respect, getting no respect.
纠结于“尊重”这个概念，觉得自己完全得不到尊重。

1125
00:52:57.920 --> 00:53:01.920
And this just sends his brain into Rodney Dangerfield land.
这让他的大脑直接进入了罗德尼·丹格菲尔德的世界。

1126
00:53:02.240 --> 00:53:08.500
So he's going to do some real kind of like off-the-cuff Rodney Dangerfield impressions,
所以他要做一些即兴的罗德尼·丹格菲尔德模仿秀，

1127
00:53:08.500 --> 00:53:16.540
which morphs into a Jeff Foxworthy impression and then Borat and then Jerry Seinfeld and then back to Rodney Dangerfield again.
接着演变成杰夫·福克斯沃西的模仿秀，然后是波拉特，然后是杰瑞·宋飞，最后又回到了罗德尼·丹格菲尔德。

1128
00:53:16.540 --> 00:53:18.660
It's a pretty epic talking head.
这是一段相当史诗级的单采。

1129
00:53:18.980 --> 00:53:19.920
It is.
确实。

1130
00:53:19.920 --> 00:53:27.340
Well, you know, Jenna, that talking head, that whole Rodney Dangerfield comic riff is not in the shooting draft.
珍娜，你知道的，那段单采，整段罗德尼·丹格菲尔德的喜剧即兴并不是拍摄剧本里的。

1131
00:53:27.520 --> 00:53:28.640
It's a whole other talking head.
那是完全不同的另一段单采。

1132
00:53:28.820 --> 00:53:29.120
Huh.
哼。

1133
00:53:29.400 --> 00:53:32.260
So I have to imagine they handed Steve a whole bunch of alts.
所以我猜他们塞给史蒂夫一大堆备选台词。

1134
00:53:32.380 --> 00:53:33.500
They would do that to us, right?
他们也会对我们这么做，对吧？

1135
00:53:34.080 --> 00:53:37.540
And this is the one that they picked because that is not the one in the script.
而这是他们选中那版，因为剧本里可不是这个。

1136
00:53:38.700 --> 00:53:38.860
Interesting.
有趣。

1137
00:53:39.340 --> 00:53:40.500
Well, I liked this one.
不过我很喜欢这一版。

1138
00:53:40.680 --> 00:53:41.300
I did, too.
我也一样。

1139
00:53:41.440 --> 00:53:43.960
And I have to think Steve improvised a little.
而且我猜史蒂夫稍微即兴发挥了一下。

1140
00:53:44.120 --> 00:53:47.300
I think it was on the page, but I can sort of see Steve doing his thing.
我觉得剧本上是有的，但我能想象到史蒂夫在展现他自己的风格。

1141
00:53:47.800 --> 00:53:48.400
I'm sure.
肯定的。

1142
00:53:48.400 --> 00:53:54.720
However, while that talking head was happening, everyone else is in the parking lot, you know, they're heading home.
然而，就在那段单采进行的同时，其他所有人都在停车场，你知道的，他们准备回家了。

1143
00:53:54.960 --> 00:54:00.380
There is a wrap-up scene of the Dwight, Andy, Angela love triangle.
有一个关于德怀特、安迪和安吉拉三角恋的收尾场景。

1144
00:54:00.900 --> 00:54:05.020
It's in the shooting draft, and it didn't make it to the deleted scenes.
它在拍摄剧本里，但没有被剪进删除片段中。

1145
00:54:05.260 --> 00:54:07.060
But Andy and Angela walk to the car.
安迪和安吉拉走向汽车。

1146
00:54:07.260 --> 00:54:13.520
They pass by Dwight, who is scraping off a Cornell sticker from the back window of the Xterra.
他们从德怀特身边走过，德怀特正在刮掉Xterra后车窗上的康奈尔大学贴纸。

1147
00:54:13.900 --> 00:54:15.980
And Andy says, goodbye, old friend.
安迪说，再见，老朋友。

1148
00:54:16.280 --> 00:54:19.960
May all your roads be downhill and the wind be on your back windshield.
愿你前路皆是下坡，顺风常拂后挡风玻璃。

1149
00:54:20.220 --> 00:54:22.020
And Angela's like, Andy.
然后安吉拉说，安迪。

1150
00:54:22.560 --> 00:54:25.340
And Andy says, I can't believe Dwight would do me like that.
安迪说，我真不敢相信德怀特会对我做出这种事。

1151
00:54:25.500 --> 00:54:27.140
He took advantage of my kindness.
他利用了我的善良。

1152
00:54:27.140 --> 00:54:30.360
And Angela says, he didn't take advantage of you.
安吉拉说，他没有利用你。

1153
00:54:30.520 --> 00:54:31.520
He bested you.
他战胜了你。

1154
00:54:31.900 --> 00:54:33.640
You were bested.
你被他击败了。

1155
00:54:33.840 --> 00:54:37.500
And then he tries to put his arm around her, and she shoves it away.
然后他想搂住她，被她一把推开了。

1156
00:54:37.680 --> 00:54:40.900
And she looks at Dwight like he's super hot.
她看着德怀特的眼神，就像觉得他超级性感一样。

1157
00:54:41.620 --> 00:54:42.020
Wow.
哇哦。

1158
00:54:42.420 --> 00:54:42.920
Yeah.
对啊。

1159
00:54:43.420 --> 00:54:48.280
Well, Angela, we should just call these deleted scenes feisty in the parking lot.
好吧，安吉拉，我们干脆把这些删减片段叫作停车场里的辣妹吧。

1160
00:54:48.280 --> 00:54:56.420
Because I know that over by Pam and Jim's car, there is a scene that we shot that I believe is in the deleted scenes.
因为我知道在潘和吉姆的车旁，我们拍过一个片段，我记得就在删减片段里。

1161
00:54:56.420 --> 00:55:05.760
Where Jim tells Pam the truth about Ryan and what Ryan said to him and that he's gunning for him to maybe get fired or put him on notice.
吉姆在那里向潘坦白了关于瑞安的真相，以及瑞安对他说的话，说瑞安正处心积虑想让他被炒鱿鱼或者给他记过警告。

1162
00:55:06.000 --> 00:55:08.180
And Pam is not having it.
而潘可不吃这一套。

1163
00:55:08.460 --> 00:55:10.420
Oh, I titled it Pam's pissed.
噢，我给它起名叫“潘发飙了”。

1164
00:55:10.780 --> 00:55:11.200
Yeah.
没错。

1165
00:55:11.560 --> 00:55:13.380
And Sam, you got to play that clip.
山姆，你得把那个片段放一下。

1166
00:55:15.100 --> 00:55:16.580
Hey, what really happened today?
嘿，今天到底发生什么事了？

1167
00:55:16.860 --> 00:55:17.240
What do you mean?
你什么意思？

1168
00:55:17.500 --> 00:55:20.380
I mean, I don't need my glasses to know when something's stressing you out.
我的意思是，我不用戴眼镜也看得出什么时候有什么事让你压力山大。

1169
00:55:20.520 --> 00:55:21.060
What happened today?
今天发生什么了？

1170
00:55:23.780 --> 00:55:25.220
Ryan is trying to get rid of me.
瑞安想甩掉我。

1171
00:55:26.480 --> 00:55:29.960
He came in today to give me an official warning about my job performance.
他今天来给我下达了关于我工作表现的正式警告。

1172
00:55:30.440 --> 00:55:30.760
What?
什么？

1173
00:55:32.040 --> 00:55:33.580
God, he's such a creep.
天哪，他真是个讨厌鬼。

1174
00:55:34.560 --> 00:55:36.100
That really pisses me off.
这真让我火大。

1175
00:55:36.740 --> 00:55:38.060
I'm going to bash his face in.
我要把他的脸砸扁。

1176
00:55:38.200 --> 00:55:40.060
I'm going to bash his face in with a stale bagel.
我要用一块放硬了的百吉饼把他的脸砸扁。

1177
00:55:40.240 --> 00:55:41.540
Then I'm going to throw a rock at his car.
然后我要朝他的车扔块石头。

1178
00:55:42.540 --> 00:55:44.100
Come on, we're going to New York right now.
走吧，我们现在就去纽约。

1179
00:55:44.220 --> 00:55:44.560
I'm driving.
我开车。

1180
00:55:44.680 --> 00:55:46.500
If I hit him without my glasses, I don't think it's a crime.
如果我不戴眼镜撞到他，我觉得这应该不算犯罪吧。

1181
00:55:47.060 --> 00:55:47.380
Great.
太棒了。

1182
00:55:48.480 --> 00:55:50.520
God, I should have told you all about this sooner.
天哪，我应该早点把这些都告诉你们的。

1183
00:55:51.000 --> 00:55:51.820
What a jerk.
真是个混蛋。

1184
00:55:51.820 --> 00:55:53.020
What a jerk.
真是个混蛋。

1185
00:55:54.600 --> 00:56:01.660
Can you imagine if they had left in the sex talk between Jim and Pam up at the top?
你能想象如果他们把一开始吉姆和潘之间关于性的话题保留下来会怎样吗？

1186
00:56:02.000 --> 00:56:07.700
And then this scene of Pam saying she's going to throw a rock at Ryan or maybe hit him with her car.
然后接着是这个场景：潘说她要向瑞安扔石头，或者可能用车载着去撞他。

1187
00:56:08.200 --> 00:56:09.460
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1188
00:56:09.600 --> 00:56:12.040
And in the shooting draft, it was much shorter.
在拍摄剧本里，这段要短得多。

1189
00:56:12.260 --> 00:56:14.100
You just said, I'm going to smash his face.
你当时只说了句“我要砸碎他的脸”。

1190
00:56:14.100 --> 00:56:15.900
And that was it, you know.
然后就没了，你知道的。

1191
00:56:15.900 --> 00:56:19.320
But in this deleted scene, Pam is going off.
但在这个删减片段里，潘彻底爆发了。

1192
00:56:19.600 --> 00:56:21.020
You do not mess with her, man.
你可千万别惹她，老兄。

1193
00:56:21.400 --> 00:56:22.300
I guess not.
我想也是吧。

1194
00:56:22.580 --> 00:56:24.720
Not after the night they had last night.
经历昨晚那种美妙夜晚之后更是如此。

1195
00:56:25.460 --> 00:56:26.980
The one night in heaven?
那如天堂般的一夜？

1196
00:56:27.360 --> 00:56:27.880
Yeah.
没错。

1197
00:56:29.980 --> 00:56:30.580
Wowzers.
哇噢。

1198
00:56:31.180 --> 00:56:35.640
Well, the tag for this episode brings us all the resolution we need.
好吧，这集的尾声给我们带来了我们需要的所有结局。

1199
00:56:35.840 --> 00:56:37.340
We're back in the conference room.
我们又回到了会议室。

1200
00:56:37.760 --> 00:56:44.900
Michael is proposing some more great ideas like a summer Christmas caroling sales event.
迈克尔又在提出一些绝妙的点子，比如夏日圣诞节唱诗销售活动。

1201
00:56:44.900 --> 00:56:46.820
He throws to Stanley.
他传球给斯坦利。

1202
00:56:47.240 --> 00:56:48.680
Stanley, what do you think?
斯坦利，你觉得怎么样？

1203
00:56:49.040 --> 00:56:53.400
Stanley says, I think it might be your best idea yet.
斯坦利说，我觉得这可能是你迄今为止最好的主意。

1204
00:56:53.900 --> 00:56:54.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1205
00:56:54.380 --> 00:56:58.660
And then Phyllis kind of laughs and says, that's the dumbest thing I've ever heard.
然后菲利斯有点嘲笑地说，这是我听过最蠢的事。

1206
00:56:59.080 --> 00:57:02.140
Michael says, everybody out except Phyllis.
迈克尔说，除了菲利斯，所有人都出去。

1207
00:57:06.540 --> 00:57:08.080
It's such a great tag.
这个结尾太棒了。

1208
00:57:08.840 --> 00:57:10.600
Guys, that was Did I Stutter?
伙计们，刚才那是《我刚才说结巴了吗》？

1209
00:57:10.800 --> 00:57:13.100
I can't believe I'm about to say this, Angela.
我真不敢相信我要说这话，安吉拉。

1210
00:57:13.280 --> 00:57:15.700
We are coming up on the end of season four.
我们快要迎来第四季的尾声了。

1211
00:57:15.700 --> 00:57:17.480
We've just got a few more episodes.
我们只剩下最后几集了。

1212
00:57:18.000 --> 00:57:18.400
I know.
我知道。

1213
00:57:18.580 --> 00:57:21.780
Last night I had to put a whole new disc in my DVD player.
昨晚我的DVD播放器得换一整张新光盘。

1214
00:57:22.280 --> 00:57:22.800
Wow.
哇。

1215
00:57:23.120 --> 00:57:26.840
You know it's serious when she's got to put a new disc in, guys.
大家注意，当她不得不换新光盘时，就说明事情严重了。

1216
00:57:27.000 --> 00:57:27.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1217
00:57:27.420 --> 00:57:30.260
I'm on my last disc for season four.
我正在看第四季的最后一张光盘。

1218
00:57:30.600 --> 00:57:32.320
It's going by so faSt.
时间过得太快了。

1219
00:57:32.560 --> 00:57:33.660
It's flying by.
时光飞逝。

1220
00:57:33.960 --> 00:57:36.040
We'll be back next week with Job Fair.
我们下周将带着《招聘会》回归。

1221
00:57:36.300 --> 00:57:38.800
Thank you to Brent Forrester and to Leslie David Baker.
感谢布伦特·福雷斯特和莱斯利·大卫·贝克。

1222
00:57:38.800 --> 00:57:41.820
Thanks for texting us back about this episode.
谢谢你们回短信跟我们讨论这一集。

1223
00:57:42.020 --> 00:57:46.520
And thanks to me for being a digital hoarder and having my shooting draft.
还要感谢我这个数码囤积狂保留着拍摄剧本。

1224
00:57:47.060 --> 00:57:47.620
Yes.
没错。

1225
00:57:47.920 --> 00:57:48.880
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

1226
00:57:49.540 --> 00:57:51.540
All right, you guys have a great week.
好了，祝大家有个愉快的一周。

1227
00:57:51.660 --> 00:57:52.520
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1228
00:57:52.520 --> 00:57:57.940
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies' Second Drink.
感谢收听《办公室女士的第二杯》。

1229
00:57:58.140 --> 00:58:01.860
This episode was initially created in collaboration with Earwolf.
本集最初是与Earwolf合作制作的。

1230
00:58:02.320 --> 00:58:06.960
Office Ladies is a presentation of Odyssey and is produced by Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》是奥德赛公司呈献的节目，由詹娜·费舍尔和安吉拉·金西制作。

1231
00:58:07.200 --> 00:58:11.940
Our executive producer is Cassie Jerkins, and our audio engineer and associate producer is
我们的执行制作人是卡西·杰金斯，我们的音频工程师兼副制作人是

1232
00:58:11.940 --> 00:58:12.780
Molly Nugent.
莫莉·纽金特。

1233
00:58:13.060 --> 00:58:15.640
Odyssey's executive producer is Leah Reese Dennis.
奥德赛公司的执行制作人是莉亚·里斯·丹尼斯。

1234
00:58:16.060 --> 00:58:18.800
Office Ladies was mixed and mastered by Bill Schultz.
《办公室女士》由比尔·舒尔茨进行混音和母带处理。

1235
00:58:18.980 --> 00:58:21.740
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿的《橡胶树》。
